---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Generator from '../../components/Generator.astro';
import StyleGallery from '../../components/StyleGallery.astro';

const title = 'Minecraft Papercraft Generator — Free Blocky Papercraft Designs';
const description = 'Generate free Minecraft-style papercraft designs with the blocky voxel papercraft generator. Describe a creeper, pickaxe, or blocky scene and get an AI papercraft design.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} ogType="website">
  <article class="container generator-page">
    <header class="generator-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="label">Minecraft Papercraft Generator</span></p>
      <h1>Generate blocky voxel papercraft</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Chunky cubes and pixel-perfect blocks for game-inspired art. Describe an idea, pick the Minecraft
        style, and generate a beautiful papercraft design for inspiration and creative exploration.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Generator app (pre-set to the Minecraft style) -->
    <Generator defaultStyle="minecraft" defaultPrompt="a blocky creeper face" />

    <StyleGallery style="minecraft" label="Minecraft" />

    <!-- SEO content -->
    <section class="gen-info reveal">
      <h2>What you can make in the Minecraft style</h2>
      <p>
        The Minecraft papercraft generator is built for chunky voxel shapes — creeper faces, pickaxes,
        swords, blocky houses, and cube-style animals. Tell it <strong>a blocky creeper face</strong>,
        <strong>a diamond pickaxe</strong>, or <strong>a voxel village house</strong>, and it returns a
        cube-based papercraft-style design you can use for inspiration.
        Every design is original papercraft-style artwork with a blocky voxel look.
      </p>

      <h2>How to use a generated design</h2>
      <ol class="gen-steps">
        <li><strong>Describe</strong> an idea above (or just press Generate for a suggestion), then pick your preferred style.</li>
        <li><strong>Generate</strong> your papercraft design — the AI creates a unique cube-style artwork in seconds.</li>
        <li><strong>Save</strong> your favorite designs for personal reference, inspiration, or creative exploration.</li>
        <li><strong>Explore</strong> different styles and variations — the same idea renders differently in Cute, Low Poly, Pixel, Fantasy, or Minecraft.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Other styles to try</h2>
      <p>
        Want a different look? The same idea renders differently in
        <a href="/tools/cute/">Cute</a>, <a href="/tools/lowpoly/">Low Poly</a>, or
        <a href="/tools/fantasy/">Fantasy</a>. Browse them all on the
        <a href="/tools/">papercraft generators hub</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="gen-faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Is the Minecraft generator free?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Every blocky papercraft design is free to generate and download. No account required.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What file do I get?</summary>
          <p>You get a high-resolution papercraft design image, ready to save and reuse as inspiration.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I make creeper or pickaxe designs?</summary>
          <p>Describe a creeper face, pickaxe, sword, blocky animal, or cube scene and the generator renders it as a voxel papercraft-style artwork.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is this an official Minecraft product?</summary>
          <p>No. koPaper is not affiliated with or endorsed by Mojang Studios or Microsoft. Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang Studios. This generator creates original blocky voxel artwork inspired by the game's cube aesthetic.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <h2>The Minecraft style, explained</h2>
      <p>
        The Minecraft style renders your idea as a blocky voxel papercraft artwork — chunky cubes, visible
        "block" facets, and a crisp grid look that reads like folded paper made from game blocks.
        It works best for subjects with strong, simple silhouettes: creeper faces, tools, weapons,
        blocky animals, buildings, and anything that suits cube geometry.
      </p>

      <h2>Example prompts that work well</h2>
      <ul class="gen-steps">
        <li><strong>a blocky creeper face</strong> — the classic, great first try</li>
        <li><strong>a diamond pickaxe</strong> — clean, instantly recognizable shape</li>
        <li><strong>a voxel village house</strong> — layered cubes, great depth</li>
        <li><strong>a blocky sword</strong> — bold silhouette, high contrast</li>
        <li><strong>a cube-style cow</strong> — fun, chunky, easy to read</li>
        <li><strong>a blocky mine scene with ore</strong> — perfect for game-themed projects</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the Minecraft style is best for</h2>
      <p>
        Use blocky voxel papercraft designs for: game-themed party decorations, YouTube thumbnails and
        channel art, pixel-art style room decor, classroom gaming themes, and sticker or badge inspiration.
        Because the look is geometric and chunky, cube designs also translate well to card and poster layouts.
      </p>

      <h2>Minecraft vs. other styles at a glance</h2>
      <table class="gen-compare">
        <tr><th>Style</th><th>Look</th><th>Best for</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Minecraft</td><td>blocky, voxel, cube-based</td><td>game themes, tools, blocky scenes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pixel</td><td>blocky, 8-bit, grid-based</td><td>game themes, retro icons, chunky subjects</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cute</td><td>round, kawaii, soft</td><td>kids' crafts, gifts, friendly mascots</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Low Poly</td><td>angular, geometric facets</td><td>architectural shapes, animals, modern decor</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fantasy</td><td>magical, luminous, ornate</td><td>castles, dragons, wizards, dream scenes</td></tr>
      </table>

      <h2>Tips for better blocky results</h2>
      <ul class="gen-steps">
        <li>Keep your subject to one main object — crowded prompts blur the cube look.</li>
        <li>Name a clear subject ("a blocky creeper face") before adding extras like colors or poses.</li>
        <li>Try the same idea in multiple styles to compare — each style changes the mood completely.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>More frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="gen-faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Do blocky designs work as printable templates?</summary>
          <p>Minecraft-style papercraft designs are inspiration artwork, not cut-and-fold templates. For printable sheet templates, see our <a href="/printables/">free printables library</a>.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use a blocky design commercially?</summary>
          <p>Generated designs are for personal inspiration and creative exploration; commercial reuse of the generator output should be checked against our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does the generator run on my phone?</summary>
          <p>Yes — the Minecraft generator works in any modern browser on desktop and mobile, with no account needed.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
    name: 'koPaper Minecraft Papercraft Generator',
    applicationCategory: 'DesignApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
    description: 'Free online tool to generate blocky voxel Minecraft-style papercraft designs from a text idea.',
  })}></script>
</BaseLayout>
